From 5cbd9b7e4f968ae0d32b55360940b72797b6d916 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stewart Addison <sxa@ibm.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:46:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [riscv] Allow vlen=1024

This resolves the remaining crashes observed in Node.js at
https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/64538 allowing execution on
systems with vlen=1024 such as the K3's A100 cores including raising
kMaxRvvVLEN from 512 to 1024.  the code has a refactored helper
function to abstract out some of the changes across the SetSimd*
functions.  The changes to the tests allow them to pass successfully in
vlen=1024 environment with functionality for lower vlen's unaffected.

Test: Run the code snippet from
https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/64538#issuecomment-5328340054 -
it will give an illegal exception on a system with a vlen of 1024
without this patch.  If someone else can test it on other systems that
would be good as I have only verified it on the K3's vlen=256 and
vlen=1024 cores (and also by building Node.js with these changes and
verifying that npm no longer crashes).

The main functional piece of the patch is quite small, but there have
been a number of changes to the unit tests required to support this
which are included in this CL.  The updated tests have been executed on
vlen sizes of 256 and 1024 and pass.

This patch was assisted by cursor AI.

R=yahan@iscas.ac.cn

